{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF12", "label": "Study family SF12: A1 within-scheme re-test controlling early-third PPP selection", "score": 2.11, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-001 auto_related_family (repeat_order_unknown) FAM:SF12", "FAM:SF-APPA-001 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF12"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "A1 within-scheme re-test controlling early-third PPP selection", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "Within the same inferred scheme (and within early-PPP quintiles), adapters improve PPP more than wrong-way teams, and this carries to the next game.", "observed_result": ["[APPA-002] Within scheme gap: DROP +0.0830 (Welch p=0.0046), HELP +0.0539 (p=0.0493), SWITCH -0.0199 (p=0.6514). Quintile gaps -0.0440, -0.0231, +0.0138, +0.0133, +0.0966. Carryover gaps DROP +0.0039 (p=0.4244), HELP -0. [cut; read_family for the full text]", "[APPS-051] DROP: adapt +0.0041 vs wrong -0.0789, gap +0.0830, Welch p=0.0046, n=73/109. HELP: +0.0943 vs +0.0404, gap +0.0539, p=0.0493, n=96/115. SWITCH: +0.1200 vs +0.1399, gap -0.0199, p=0.6514, n=36/50. Pooled quinti [cut; read_family for the full text]"], "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)"}, "relationships": []}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-001", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-001: A1 adaptation falsification: asymmetry, confidence and carryover tests", "score": 1.75, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPA-001 (0.73)", "FAM:SF13 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF-APPA-001"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "A1 adaptation falsification: asymmetry, confidence and carryover tests", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "If the A1 adapter PPP lift is real coverage response, wrong-way teams should do worse than no-signal teams, the gap should widen with scheme-vote confidence, and adapting in Game N should carry over to Game N+1.", "observed_result": "T1 dPPP